{"kind":"text","seq":34,"text":"Best banked score this round is confirmed at 7.10, up from 6.9 last round.\n\nFour builds this round, all closed circuits and none crashed:\n\n| Build | Excitement | Intensity | Length | Inversions |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Short west loop | 6.41 | 9.24 | 553 | 3 |\n| Plus northern extension | 6.94 | 10.11 | 943 | 3 |\n| Loop moved before the turn | 6.92 | 8.13 | 944 | 3 |\n| Taller second lift into a second loop | 7.10 | 8.62 | 1014 | 4 |\n\nThe winning layout is a counter-clockwise circuit west of the lake: a 13-piece chain lift on y=60 into a 60-degree drop, straight into a vertical loop, a banked turn south, an airtime hill, a corkscrew, then a boosted half-loop exiting through a corkscrew down as a dive-loop. It returns east along y=52, north at x=64, then a second 11-piece lift on y=74 drops into a second vertical loop before hills bring it back along y=64 to the station. Similarity to the stock library is 0.37, below the penalty threshold. Nothing was named or coloured, as instructed.\n\nBest coaster: 167-piece twister with two lifts and four inversions, excitement 7.10, intensity 8.62, nausea 4.64."}
